1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,540
This is Causabee.

2
00:00:01,690 --> 00:00:08,160
Mail, letters, documents, screenshots —
it turns all the pieces into clear matters.

3
00:00:08,860 --> 00:00:16,570
Let’s follow one of them — Mum’s care, after her fall —
through one day, on the Mac, the iPad, and the iPhone.

4
00:00:17,240 --> 00:00:19,330
In the morning, you open your Mac.

5
00:00:19,520 --> 00:00:24,220
With Auto on, Causabee has already
fetched the new mail, and read it.

6
00:00:24,830 --> 00:00:31,000
Before anything went to the AI, names and numbers
were swapped for placeholders, right on your Mac.

7
00:00:31,330 --> 00:00:35,750
Dr. Brandt became Person A,
and Helga became Person B.

8
00:00:36,080 --> 00:00:39,100
The AI only ever sees the disguise.

9
00:00:39,800 --> 00:00:43,310
All that’s left for you is the last step: take it in.

10
00:00:43,970 --> 00:00:48,200
The two mails land in Mum’s matter,
and they bring a new task with them.

11
00:00:48,870 --> 00:00:52,980
Every matter has one next step,
and the reason it can’t wait.

12
00:00:53,580 --> 00:00:59,600
Below it are the tasks: whose each one is,
when it’s due, and which mail it came from.

13
00:01:00,290 --> 00:01:03,430
In the afternoon, you’re at Mum’s, with the iPad.

14
00:01:03,730 --> 00:01:04,740
Tick off what’s done.

15
00:01:07,370 --> 00:01:11,970
Through your own iCloud, it’s ticked off
on your iPhone and your Mac as well.

16
00:01:12,770 --> 00:01:13,850
There’s paper, too.

17
00:01:14,300 --> 00:01:18,750
A letter from Mum’s health insurer:
her own share of the hospital stay.

18
00:01:19,450 --> 00:01:20,750
Scan it with your iPhone.

19
00:01:21,380 --> 00:01:24,400
Causabee reads it,
files the letter in Mum’s matter,

20
00:01:24,450 --> 00:01:28,400
and turns it into a task:
pay her share by the end of the month.

21
00:01:29,550 --> 00:01:32,310
On the way home, pull down on your iPhone.

22
00:01:32,510 --> 00:01:37,350
The bee flies in, fetches your mail,
and sorts each one into its matter.

23
00:01:38,010 --> 00:01:41,870
Then just ask: what do I need to do
before Tuesday’s visit?

24
00:01:42,580 --> 00:01:44,760
The answer comes with its sources.

25
00:01:44,810 --> 00:01:48,440
And a good suggestion becomes a task, with one tap.

26
00:01:49,100 --> 00:01:52,300
In the evening, back at the Mac, it’s all there:

27
00:01:52,500 --> 00:01:56,310
what you ticked off on the iPad,
and what you added on the iPhone.

28
00:01:56,510 --> 00:01:58,950
Your mail stays in your mail account.

29
00:01:59,100 --> 00:02:03,050
Your documents and your matters go with you,
through your own iCloud.

30
00:02:03,590 --> 00:02:07,130
Causabee. Be organized. Be private.
